      found 0 vulnerabilities (after adding @playwright/test + @axe-core/playwright)

## 5. A false alarm, and what it actually was

One `wizard has no serious/critical axe violations - en` run failed with
"Test timeout of 30000ms exceeded" (39.6s actual), not an axe violation -
six sequential full-page axe scans in one test is legitimately more work
than the default 30s budget assumes, and under this suite's normal
4-worker parallelism it occasionally ran past it from CPU contention alone.
Fixed by giving that specific test `test.setTimeout(60_000)` rather than
raising the whole suite's default or, worse, weakening the assertion.
Re-ran the full suite three consecutive times after the fix: 29/29 every
time.

## 6. Components built and wired in (not just demoed)

`Button`/`IconButton` (`desktop/src/components/Button.tsx`) - replaces
`.wizard-btn`/`-ghost`/`-primary`, which turned out to be used well beyond
the wizard (`SourceBanner`, `AgentChoiceStep`, `Evidence`, `Settings` all
had their own copies of the same three classes). All 14 button call sites
across 5 files now use one component with 4 variants
(primary/secondary/ghost/danger).

`TechnicalValue` (`desktop/src/components/TechnicalValue.tsx`) - a real
`<bdi>`-based replacement for the `<span className="ltr-field">` pattern
hand-applied at each call site; wired into `SourceBanner`, `AgentChoiceStep`,
`Evidence`, `Settings` (11 call sites) in place of the raw span. Copy-to-
clipboard and truncation/tooltip (the rest of §4.9's spec for this
component) are deliberately deferred to Phase 5, where Diagnostics'
copy-with-feedback requirement actually needs them - not half-built here.

Not yet done (honestly tracked, not silently dropped): the full 18-component
list, an internal showcase route, dropping `'unsafe-inline'` from CSP, and
the remaining ~30 inline `style={{...}}` occurrences not touched by this
pass (Evidence.tsx alone still has several - marginTop/color/fontSize
inline styles this pass did not touch, since it was scoped to buttons and
technical values specifically, not a full page rebuild).

